= Hash function — Simple =

A hash function turns data into a compact value called a hash or digest. The same input gives the same output. Cryptographic hash functions are designed so that reversing the hash or deliberately finding matching inputs is computationally difficult.

'''Important boundary:''' hash function ≠ encryption.

